{"name":"Cleopatra’s Gown","hex":"#795088","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cleopatra","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The butterfly Gonepteryx cleopatra of the family Pieridae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cleopatra"},{"term":"gown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A loose, flowing upper garment.","A woman's ordinary outer dress, such as a calico or silk gown."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To dress in a gown, to don or garb with a gown."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gown","blocks":[{"text":"A gown, from the Latin word, gunna, is a usually loose outer garment from knee-to-full-length worn by people of both sexes in Europe from the Early Middle Ages to the 17th century, and continuing today in certain professions; later, the term gown was applied to any full-length woman's garment consisting of a bodice and an attached skirt. A long, loosely fitted gown called a Banyan was worn by men in the 18th century as an informal coat."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Ball_gown_MET_DT7579.jpg/330px-Ball_gown_MET_DT7579.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gown","wikidata":"Q1036729"},{"title":"Cleopatra","blocks":[{"text":"Cleopatra VII Thea Philopator was Queen of the Ptolemaic Kingdom of Egypt from 51 to 30 BC, and the last active Hellenistic pharaoh. A member of the Ptolemaic dynasty, she was a descendant of its founder, Ptolemy I Soter, a Macedonian Greek general and companion of Alexander the Great. Cleopatra's first language was Koine Greek, and she is the only Ptolemaic ruler known to have learned the Egyptian language, among several others. After her death, Egypt became a province of the Roman Empire, marking the end of the Hellenistic period, which had begun with the death of Alexander in 323 BC."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Kleopatra-VII.-Altes-Museum-Berlin1.jpg/330px-Kleopatra-VII.-Altes-Museum-Berlin1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cleopatra","wikidata":"Q635"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Cleopatra_signature_bw.jpg/500px-Cleopatra_signature_bw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Cleopatra_signature_bw.jpg/500px-Cleopatra_signature_bw.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACleopatra_signature_bw.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Cleopatra_VII%2C_dalla_via_appia_tra_ariccia_e_genzano%2C_40-30_ac_ca._01.JPG/500px-Cleopatra_VII%2C_dalla_via_appia_tra_ariccia_e_genzano%2C_40-30_ac_ca._01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Cleopatra_VII%2C_dalla_via_appia_tra_ariccia_e_genzano%2C_40-30_ac_ca._01.JPG/1280px-Cleopatra_VII%2C_dalla_via_appia_tra_ariccia_e_genzano%2C_40-30_ac_ca._01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Cleopatra_VII%2C_dalla_via_appia_tra_ariccia_e_genzano%2C_40-30_ac_ca._01.JPG/500px-Cleopatra_VII%2C_dalla_via_appia_tra_ariccia_e_genzano%2C_40-30_ac_ca._01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACleopatra_VII%2C_dalla_via_appia_tra_ariccia_e_genzano%2C_40-30_ac_ca._01.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Ptolemy_XII_Auletes_Louvre_Ma3449.jpg/500px-Ptolemy_XII_Auletes_Louvre_Ma3449.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https: